cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the version and note the informal AI-review status."
title: "Realizable Nearlinear-Gap Hardness for Small Monotone Formulas"
authors:
  - name: "Quantyra Research"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/Quantyra/realizable-cmmsa-hardness"
abstract: >-
  For every sufficiently large fixed leaf bound L, randomized polynomial-time
  many-one NP-hardness of realizable weighted CMMSA with gap L^(1-o(1)) and
  vanishing NO satisfaction threshold, with the corresponding fixed-advice
  learning corollary through Hirahara--Nanashima. The polynomial exponent
  may depend on L. Earlier realizable hardness is credited to Hirahara;
  the contribution is the nearlinear exponent. Informal AI review; no
  human peer review or machine-checked proof, and no priority certification.
keywords:
  - hardness of approximation
  - monotone formulas
  - realizable learning
  - probabilistically checkable proofs
